!!id:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/32/app/orders-api-2.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/32/ltr8/http/meta-http-2.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/meta-kernel.tn"
@doc:"""
  The orders service described as types: one schema, ONE import, no type constructors.

  The single !!import is meta-kernel, for top, text, integer, uri and void. One import, so
  UPSTREAM #11 never arises. The !!meta is meta-http-2.tn, which exists only to declare the
  annotation types -- see its own @doc for why they cannot live here.

  An operation is `top & { ... }`. top is the root, so an entry that is neither product nor sum
  describes no data value -- nobody can write !create_order { } and mean anything. It is
  meta-kernel's own device for reference and instance_template, and it needs no ~.

  Payload types sit in FIELD TYPE positions, so the resolver resolves and checks them:
  `request: order` is a reference, and naming a type that does not exist fails to load. That is the
  property api-1.tn cannot have, where a payload was { schema: uri  type: text } and nothing ever
  looked either string up.

  The convention, which is convention and not enforcement:
    - a field annotated @status is a response; its type is that response's body
    - a field annotated @parameter is a parameter; its type is the parameter's type
    - the field named `request` is the request body; an operation without one omits it
  """
{
  order => { sku: text  quantity: integer }

  @doc:"Abbreviated; the shipping one is problem-2.tn, which follows RFC 9457."
  problem => { type: uri?  title: text  status: integer  detail: text? }

  @doc:"A business error: schema-valid, and the domain still said no. Composes problem (§5.8)."
  sku_not_found => problem & { missing_sku: text }

  create_order => @method:POST @path:"/orders" @doc:"Accept an order and confirm it." top & {
    request: order

    @status:201 created: order
    @status:400 invalid: problem
    @status:404 no_such_sku: sku_not_found
  }

  get_schema => @method:GET @path:"/schemas/{schema_path}" @doc:"Fetch a published schema." top & {
    @parameter:PATH schema_path: text

    @doc:"A schema document is not a TSON value type; void says so rather than lying."
    @status:200 found: void
    @status:404 missing: problem
  }
}
